<symbol type="2" id="120" code="505.1" name="Unpaved footpath or track, footprint: 1.4 m"><description>An unpaved footpath or rough vehicle track is a way for passing mainly by foot, without a smooth, hard surface.</description><line_symbol color="14" line_width="438" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="2500" break_length="313" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><borders><border color="15" width="125" shift="63" dashed="true" dash_length="2500" break_length="313"/></borders></line_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="121" code="505.2" name="Unpaved footpath or track, footprint: 2 m"><description>An unpaved footpath or rough vehicle track is a way for passing mainly by foot, without a smooth, hard surface.</description><line_symbol color="14" line_width="625" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="2500" break_length="313" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><borders><border color="15" width="125" shift="63" dashed="true" dash_length="2500" break_length="313"/></borders></line_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="122" code="506" name="Small unpaved footpath or track"><description>A small unpaved footpath or track.
Minimum length (isolated): two dashes (3.4 mm - footprint 13.6 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="338" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="5000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="1875" break_length="463" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="123" code="507" name="Less distinct small path"><description>A less distinct path or forestry extraction track.
Minimum length: two sections of double dashes (7.9 mm - footprint 31.6 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="338" minimum_length="9875" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="5000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="1875" break_length="1875" dashes_in_group="2" in_group_break_length="463" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="124" code="508" name="Narrow ride"><description>A distinct ride is a linear break in the forest (usually in a plantation), which does not have a distinct path along it. Where there is a path along a ride, the symbol Small unpaved footpath or track (506) shall be used.
Minimum length: two dashes (9.75 mm - footprint 39 m).</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="263" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="5000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5625" break_length="938" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol>
<symbol type="16" id="125" code="509.1" name="Railway"><description>A railway is a permanent track laid with rails on which locomotives, carriages or wagons can travel.
If it is forbidden to cross or run along the railroad, the forbidden area around the railway shall be represented with symbol Area that shall not be entered (520).
Minimum length (isolated): two dashes (4 mm - footprint 16 m).</description><combined_symbol parts="2"><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="515.1.2" name="Railway helper: inner black dashes"><line_symbol color="2" line_width="438" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" dashed="true" segment_length="3750" end_length="1875" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="1250" break_length="1250" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol></part><part private="true"><symbol type="2" code="515.1.1" name="Railway helper: black border, white background"><line_symbol color="4" line_width="438" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="3750" end_length="1875" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="1875" break_length="1250" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><borders><border color="2" width="125" shift="0"/></borders></line_symbol></symbol></part></combined_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="126" code="509.2" name="Tramway"><description>A tramway is a public vehicle running regularly along certain streets, usually on rails. The track can be easily crossed by the competitor.
Tramways are generally not represented. However, if they serve navigation or orientation, they can be represented.</description><line_symbol color="-1" line_width="375" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="3750" end_length="1875" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="1875" break_length="1250" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><borders><border color="10" width="125" shift="0"/></borders></line_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="127" code="510" name="Power line, cableway or skilift"><description>Power line, cableway or skilift.
The bars indicate the exact location of the pylons. If a section of a power line, cableway or skilift goes along a road or path (and does not offer significant additional navigational value) it should be omitted.

&lt;b&gt;Note: When drawing this symbol, press space to toggle placing the pylon symbols at new nodes.&lt;/b&gt;</description><line_symbol color="2" line_width="175" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5000" break_length="1250" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><dash_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="Dash symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1250" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="1"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="2" line_width="175" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5000" break_length="1250" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">0 -375;0 375;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol></dash_symbol></line_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="128" code="511" name="Major power line"><description>Major power lines should be drawn with a double line. The gap between the lines may indicate the extent of the powerline. Very large carrying masts shall be represented in plan shape using symbol Building (521) or High tower (524). In this case, the cable lines can be left out (the map shows only the pylons).

&lt;b&gt;Note: When drawing this symbol, press space to toggle placing the pylon symbols at new nodes.&lt;/b&gt;</description><line_symbol color="-1" line_width="1875" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5000" break_length="1250" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"><dash_symbol><symbol type="1" code="" name="Dash symbol"><point_symbol rotatable="true" inner_radius="1250" inner_color="-1" outer_width="0" outer_color="-1" elements="1"><element><symbol type="2" code=""><line_symbol color="2" line_width="250" minimum_length="0" join_style="1" cap_style="0" start_offset="0" end_offset="0" segment_length="5000" end_length="0" show_at_least_one_symbol="true" minimum_mid_symbol_count="0" minimum_mid_symbol_count_when_closed="0" dash_length="5000" break_length="1250" dashes_in_group="1" in_group_break_length="625" mid_symbols_per_spot="1" mid_symbol_distance="0"/></symbol><object type="1"><coords count="2">0 -1400;0 1400;</coords><pattern rotation="0"><coord x="0" y="0"/></pattern></object></element></point_symbol></symbol></dash_symbol><borders><border color="2" width="175" shift="88"/></borders></line_symbol></symbol>
<symbol type="2" id="129" code="511.1" name="Major power line with pylons"><description>Major power lines should be drawn with a double line. The gap between the lines may indicate the extent of the powerline. Very large carrying masts shall be represented in plan shape using symbol Building (521) or High tower (524). In this case, the cable lines can be left out (the map shows only the pylons).

